 the text says \"after the migration is merged and Vercel is confirmed working.\" The step ordering is misleading. **Accept — reorder Phase 8.**\n\n**Review Item 7 (docs/.gitignore)** — I verified: there is no `.gitignore` inside `nextra-site/`. The `.gitignore` is at the `hankweave-docs/` root level. Since Step 1.1 copies `nextra-site/*` into `docs/`, no `.gitignore` is carried over. The review's concern is based on an inference (\"standard Next.js projects have one\"), not on reading the actual file. **Disagree — non-issue, but add a clarifying note to the plan.**\n\n**Review Item 8 (docsAvailable comment precision)** — The review is right that the guard checks `docs/public/` not `docs/`. The plan's proposed comment says \"in case `docs/` is missing\" — this is imprecise. **Accept — make comment more precise.**\n\n**Review Item 9 (Assumption #1 on history preservation)** — The plan's Step 1.1 already says \"a simple file copy with a descriptive commit is simpler\" as the alternative and frames it as the default. But Assumption #1 at the top could be more explicit. **Accept — tighten assumption wording.**\n\n**Review Item 10 (bunfig.toml verification)** — I verified the file. It only has `[test.env]` with `BUN_TEST = \"true\"`. This sets an env var during test runs. The `[test]` section in Bun config applies to `bun test` runs — it doesn't affect workspace behavior or `bun install`. However, `bun test` from root might pick up test files from `docs/` if not scoped. Let me check if there's a test pattern defined."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":286,"cache_read_input_tokens":82411,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":286},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a5d48287-fa06-41ff-8c53-7bb7d1a349eb","uuid":"117c9c70-96f2-4619-9a7a-a302d01c905e","timestamp":"2026-