{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012tB9PkAXJtTTMfUp6mvUBv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good. The `test:unit` script explicitly runs `bun test tests/unit` — scoped to the `tests/unit` directory. Same for integration and e2e. So `bunfig.toml`'s `[test.env]` applies to `bun test` runs, but the test scripts are already path-scoped and won't pick up docs files. The `bunfig.toml` concern is minor but worth a brief verification note. **Accept as a minor note.**\n\nNow I also want to check the remaining review items I haven't explicitly covered:\n\n- **Item 11 (smoke test convention)** — Review says no issue, just confirming conventions match. No change needed.\n- **Item 12 (CI changes / bun.lock)** — Overlaps with item 3. Already covered.\n- **Item 13 (SOP line 40)** — Review confirms the plan's proposed wording is correct. No change needed beyond what's already there.\n- **Item 14 (bunfig.toml)** — Same as item 10. Covered above.\n- **Item 15 (docsAvailable always true)** — Plan's treatment is already reasonable. The comment update addresses this.\n- **Item 16 (Step 8.1 ordering)** — Same as item 6.\n- **Item 17 (docs/.gitignore)** — Same as item 7.\n- **Item 18 (Assumption #1 precision)** — Same as item 9.\n\nThe additional review items (1-6 in the body, beyond the summary 10) that contain observations but no required action:\n- **Review Section 1 (line number checks)** — All confirmed correct.\n- **Review Section 3 (.gitignore analysis)** — The review notes the plan should state explicitly that unscoped patterns cover tree-wide. **Accept as clarification.**\n- **Review Section 6 (docs/ vs docs in INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP)** — Confirmed correct. Informational only. The plan already addresses the `startsWith` check.\n\nNow I have a complete assessment. Let me start making the plan edits."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1080,"cache_r