{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DMtJNDQe3Ge9usLVRF2tSZ","type":"tool_result","content":"   648→**Alternative (optimization)**: If the team prefers the cleaner setup of `docs/` as root directory, try it after the primary approach is confirmed working. With \"Root Directory\" set to `docs/`, Vercel typically checks out the full repo but sets the working directory to `docs/`. Bun should then traverse upward to find the workspace root. If this works, it is the slightly cleaner configuration — but test it explicitly before relying on it.\n   649→\n   650→**Step 7.3: Configure \"Ignored Build Step\" (recommended)**\n   651→\n   652→To prevent unnecessary docs rebuilds when only runtime code changes:\n   653→1. Go to Settings -> General -> \"Ignored Build Step\"\n   654→2. Set to: `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/`\n   655→\n   656→This tells Vercel to skip the build if no files under `docs/` have changed.\n   657→\n   658→**Caveat**: Vercel may perform shallow clones for deployments. If `HEAD^` is not available in a shallow clone, this command will fail. In that case, Vercel would proceed with the build (the command exits non-zero, which Vercel treats as \"do not skip\"). This is a safe failure mode — Vercel builds unnecessarily rather than skipping a needed build. If this becomes a problem (frequent unnecessary builds), the more robust alternative is to use Vercel's environment variable approach: a custom script that checks `VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA` against the previous deployment.\n   659→\n   660→**Step 7.4: Configure branch deployment**\n   661→\n   662→The monorepo uses `develop` and `release/alpha` branches. Configure Vercel:\n   663→- Production deployment: whichever branch the docs should deploy from (likely `develop` or `release/alpha`, depending on team preference)\n   664→- Preview deployments: PRs targeting `develop`\n   665→\n   666→### Phase 8: Commit, PR, and cleanup\n   667→\n   668→**Step 8.1: Commit the migration**\n   669→\n   670→Commit all changes on the feature branch. Ensure the regenerated `bun.lock` is staged — without it, CI's `bun install --frozen-lockfile` will fail on the first run after the PR is opened.\n   671→\n   672→```bash\n   673→git add bun.lock\n   674→```\n   675→\n   676→Commit message:\n   677→```\n   678→Migrate to monorepo: bring docs into workspace\n   679→\n   680→- Add docs/ workspace (formerly SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs)\n   681→- Add \"workspaces\" field to root package.json\n   682→- Regenerate bun.lock as unified workspace lockfile\n   683→- Exclude docs/**/* from root tsconfig.json\n   684→- Update generate-schemas.ts to use monorepo-local docs path\n   685→- Add docs/ to strip lists (sync-public.ts, release.ts, test-sync-local.ts)\n   686→- Strip \"workspaces\" from public package.json in transformPackageJson()\n   687→- Update release.ts schema handling for docs/public/schemas/\n   688→- Add --exclude='docs' to test-sync-local.ts rsync\n   689→- Update .gitignore for docs build artifacts\n   690→- Update standard-operating-procedures.md\n   691→```\n   692→\n   693→**Step 8.2: Open PR targeting develop**\n   694→\n   695→Follow the existing PR conventions per SOP Section 4:\n   696→- Title: `Monorepo migration: consolidate hankweave-docs into workspace`\n   697→- Body: Problem/approach/files-changed format\n   698→\n   699→**Step 8.3: Optional CHANGELOG entry**\n   700→\n   701→Under `[Unreleased] > Changed`:\n   702→```markdown\n   703→- **Monorepo migration** -- Consolidated documentation site into the development repository as a Bun workspace. No changes to runtime behavior or public-facing interfaces.\n   704→```\n   705→\n   706→This is optional since it's an internal infrastructure change, not user-facing.\n   707→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a5d48287-fa06-41ff-8c53-7bb7d1a349eb","uuid":"0b5266d4-4c5c-49bf-97eb-69e7ffd93980","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"**Alternative (optimization)**: If the team prefers the cleaner setup of `docs/` as root directory, try it after the primary approach is confirmed working. With \"Root Directory\" set to `docs/`, Vercel typically checks out the full repo but sets the working directory to `docs/`. Bun should then traverse upward to find the workspace root. If this works, it is the slightly cleaner configuration — but test it explicitly before relying on it.\n\n**Step 7.3: Configure \"Ignored Build Step\" (recommended)**\n\nTo prevent unnecessary docs rebuilds when only runtime code changes:\n1. Go to Settings -> General -> \"Ignored Build Step\"\n2. Set to: `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/`\n\nThis tells Vercel to skip the build if no files under `docs/` have changed.\n\n**Caveat**: Vercel may perform shallow clones for deployments. If `HEAD^` is not available in a shallow clone, this command will fail. In that case, Vercel would proceed with the build (the command exits non-zero, which Vercel treats as \"do not skip\"). This is a safe failure mode — Vercel builds unnecessarily rather than skipping a needed build. If this becomes a problem (frequent unnecessary builds), the more robust alternative is to use Vercel's environment variable approach: a custom script that checks `VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA` against the previous deployment.\n\n**Step 7.4: Configure branch deployment**\n\nThe monorepo uses `develop` and `release/alpha` branches. Configure Vercel:\n- Production deployment: whichever branch the docs should deploy from (likely `develop` or `release/alpha`, depending on team preference)\n- Preview deployments: PRs targeting `develop`\n\n### Phase 8: Commit, PR, and cleanup\n\n**Step 8.1: Commit the migration**\n\nCommit all changes on the feature branch. Ensure the regenerated `bun.lock` is staged — without it, CI's `bun install --frozen-lockfile` will fail on the first run after the PR is opened.\n\n```bash\ngit add bun.lock\n```\n\nCommit message:\n```\nMigrate to monorepo: bring docs into workspace\n\n- Add docs/ workspace (formerly SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs)\n- Add \"workspaces\" field to root package.json\n- Regenerate bun.lock as unified workspace lockfile\n- Exclude docs/**/* from root tsconfig.json\n- Update generate-schemas.ts to use monorepo-local docs path\n- Add docs/ to strip lists (sync-public.ts, release.ts, test-sync-local.ts)\n- Strip \"workspaces\" from public package.json in transformPackageJson()\n- Update release.ts schema handling for docs/public/schemas/\n- Add --exclude='docs' to test-sync-local.ts rsync\n- Update .gitignore for docs build artifacts\n- Update standard-operating-procedures.md\n```\n\n**Step 8.2: Open PR targeting develop**\n\nFollow the existing PR conventions per SOP Section 4:\n- Title: `Monorepo migration: consolidate hankweave-docs into workspace`\n- Body: Problem/approach/files-changed format\n\n**Step 8.3: Optional CHANGELOG entry**\n\nUnder `[Unreleased] > Changed`:\n```markdown\n- **Monorepo migration** -- Consolidated documentation site into the development repository as a Bun workspace. No changes to runtime behavior or public-facing interfaces.\n```\n\nThis is optional since it's an internal infrastructure change, not user-facing.\n","numLines":60,"startLine":648,"totalLines":872}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:57:40.396Z"}
