{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GumzynBZW9UwpB9pkyKb4z","type":"tool_result","content":"   206→**Step 1.1: Create the `docs/` directory**\n   207→\n   208→Copy the contents of `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` into `docs/` at the runtime repo root. The files to bring in:\n   209→\n   210→```\n   211→app/\n   212→components/\n   213→content/\n   214→public/\n   215→styles/\n   216→bun.lock           (will be removed in step 1.3)\n   217→mdx-components.tsx\n   218→next-env.d.ts\n   219→next.config.mjs\n   220→package.json\n   221→tsconfig.json\n   222→vercel.json\n   223→```\n   224→\n   225→Do NOT copy the outer `hankweave-docs/` wrapper (`notes/`, `plan/`). Optionally include `hankweave-docs/README.md` as `docs/README.md` for internal reference.\n   226→\n   227→Note: the `hankweave-docs` repo's `.gitignore` lives at the outer wrapper level (`hankweave-docs/.gitignore`), not inside `nextra-site/`. Since we are copying `nextra-site/*` into `docs/`, no `.gitignore` is carried over. The root `.gitignore` already covers the relevant patterns (see Phase 4).\n   228→\n   229→If git history preservation is desired, use `git subtree add`:\n   230→```bash\n   231→git remote add -f hankweave-docs <url>\n   232→git merge -s ours --no-commit --allow-unrelated-histories hankweave-docs/main\n   233→git read-tree --prefix=docs/ -u hankweave-docs/main\n   234→git commit -m \"Merge hankweave-docs into monorepo as docs workspace\"\n   235→```\n   236→Then restructure: move `docs/nextra-site/*` up to `docs/` and remove `docs/notes/`, `docs/plan/`, `docs/README.md`, `docs/.gitignore`.\n   237→\n   238→Alternatively, a simple file copy with a descriptive commit is simpler and the docs repo history remains available in the original repo if ever needed.\n   239→\n   240→**Step 1.2: Add workspace configuration to root `package.json`**\n   241→\n   242→Add the `\"workspaces\"` field to `source/hankweave/package.json`. Place it after `\"engines\"` and before `\"scripts\"`, adjacent to other structural metadata fields. The current field order is: `name`, `version`, `description`, `author`, `keywords`, `homepage`, `type`, `publishConfig`, `bin`, `main`, `files`, `engines`, `scripts`, `devDependencies`, `peerDependencies`, `dependencies`. The result:\n   243→\n   244→```json\n   245→{\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a5d48287-fa06-41ff-8c53-7bb7d1a349eb","uuid":"c10376c3-3398-4dce-8e57-c1b28022bc7e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"**Step 1.1: Create the `docs/` directory**\n\nCopy the contents of `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` into `docs/` at the runtime repo root. The files to bring in:\n\n```\napp/\ncomponents/\ncontent/\npublic/\nstyles/\nbun.lock           (will be removed in step 1.3)\nmdx-components.tsx\nnext-env.d.ts\nnext.config.mjs\npackage.json\ntsconfig.json\nvercel.json\n```\n\nDo NOT copy the outer `hankweave-docs/` wrapper (`notes/`, `plan/`). Optionally include `hankweave-docs/README.md` as `docs/README.md` for internal reference.\n\nNote: the `hankweave-docs` repo's `.gitignore` lives at the outer wrapper level (`hankweave-docs/.gitignore`), not inside `nextra-site/`. Since we are copying `nextra-site/*` into `docs/`, no `.gitignore` is carried over. The root `.gitignore` already covers the relevant patterns (see Phase 4).\n\nIf git history preservation is desired, use `git subtree add`:\n```bash\ngit remote add -f hankweave-docs <url>\ngit merge -s ours --no-commit --allow-unrelated-histories hankweave-docs/main\ngit read-tree --prefix=docs/ -u hankweave-docs/main\ngit commit -m \"Merge hankweave-docs into monorepo as docs workspace\"\n```\nThen restructure: move `docs/nextra-site/*` up to `docs/` and remove `docs/notes/`, `docs/plan/`, `docs/README.md`, `docs/.gitignore`.\n\nAlternatively, a simple file copy with a descriptive commit is simpler and the docs repo history remains available in the original repo if ever needed.\n\n**Step 1.2: Add workspace configuration to root `package.json`**\n\nAdd the `\"workspaces\"` field to `source/hankweave/package.json`. Place it after `\"engines\"` and before `\"scripts\"`, adjacent to other structural metadata fields. The current field order is: `name`, `version`, `description`, `author`, `keywords`, `homepage`, `type`, `publishConfig`, `bin`, `main`, `files`, `engines`, `scripts`, `devDependencies`, `peerDependencies`, `dependencies`. The result:\n\n```json\n{","numLines":40,"startLine":206,"totalLines":872}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:59:18.164Z"}
