{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QrKZmWeFFLCZaZ8WcUsK5d","type":"tool_result","content":"   340→Verify schemas are written to both `schemas/` (runtime's local copy for npm) and `docs/public/schemas/` (docs site's static files).\n   341→\n   342→### Phase 3: Update strip lists for public sync\n   343→\n   344→This phase has four changes across three scripts, plus an update to the `transformPackageJson()` function. All serve the same purpose: ensure the docs workspace doesn't leak into the public mirror.\n   345→\n   346→**Step 3.1: Update `scripts/sync-public.ts` `STRIP_DIRS`**\n   347→\n   348→At line 28, add `\"docs\"`:\n   349→```typescript\n   350→const STRIP_DIRS = [\"intermediates\", \"external-docs\", \"public-release-files\", \".github/actions\", \"docs\"];\n   351→```\n   352→\n   353→This single constant change covers three consumers in the script: `prepareSnapshot()` (line 214, which builds rsync excludes with trailing slashes from `STRIP_DIRS`), `initialSync()` (lines 291–302, which iterates `STRIP_DIRS` to `rm -rf` each directory from the public clone), and `snapshotSync()`. The implementing agent does not need to touch any of these functions — they all read from the shared `STRIP_DIRS` constant.\n   354→\n   355→**Step 3.2: Update `scripts/sync-public.ts` `transformPackageJson()`**\n   356→\n   357→At line 173-196 in the `transformPackageJson()` function, add a line to delete the `\"workspaces\"` field from the public `package.json`:\n   358→\n   359→```typescript\n   360→async function transformPackageJson(packagePath: string): Promise<void> {\n   361→  const content = await readFile(packagePath, \"utf-8\");\n   362→  const pkg = JSON.parse(content);\n   363→\n   364→  pkg.name = \"hankweave\";\n   365→  pkg.publishConfig = { access: \"public\" };\n   366→  pkg.homepage = \"https://github.com/SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime\";\n   367→\n   368→  // Remove monorepo-only fields that don't apply to the public repo\n   369→  delete pkg.workspaces;\n   370→\n   371→  // Remove scripts that reference stripped internal files\n   372→  if (pkg.scripts) {\n   373→    for (const script of STRIP_SCRIPTS) {\n   374→      delete pkg.scripts[script];\n   375→    }\n   376→  }\n   377→\n   378→  await writeFile(packagePath, JSON.stringify(pkg, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n   379→  // ... logging\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a5d48287-fa06-41ff-8c53-7bb7d1a349eb","uuid":"7d81f42b-6938-4455-b1a0-e96df78e099b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"Verify schemas are written to both `schemas/` (runtime's local copy for npm) and `docs/public/schemas/` (docs site's static files).\n\n### Phase 3: Update strip lists for public sync\n\nThis phase has four changes across three scripts, plus an update to the `transformPackageJson()` function. All serve the same purpose: ensure the docs workspace doesn't leak into the public mirror.\n\n**Step 3.1: Update `scripts/sync-public.ts` `STRIP_DIRS`**\n\nAt line 28, add `\"docs\"`:\n```typescript\nconst STRIP_DIRS = [\"intermediates\", \"external-docs\", \"public-release-files\", \".github/actions\", \"docs\"];\n```\n\nThis single constant change covers three consumers in the script: `prepareSnapshot()` (line 214, which builds rsync excludes with trailing slashes from `STRIP_DIRS`), `initialSync()` (lines 291–302, which iterates `STRIP_DIRS` to `rm -rf` each directory from the public clone), and `snapshotSync()`. The implementing agent does not need to touch any of these functions — they all read from the shared `STRIP_DIRS` constant.\n\n**Step 3.2: Update `scripts/sync-public.ts` `transformPackageJson()`**\n\nAt line 173-196 in the `transformPackageJson()` function, add a line to delete the `\"workspaces\"` field from the public `package.json`:\n\n```typescript\nasync function transformPackageJson(packagePath: string): Promise<void> {\n  const content = await readFile(packagePath, \"utf-8\");\n  const pkg = JSON.parse(content);\n\n  pkg.name = \"hankweave\";\n  pkg.publishConfig = { access: \"public\" };\n  pkg.homepage = \"https://github.com/SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime\";\n\n  // Remove monorepo-only fields that don't apply to the public repo\n  delete pkg.workspaces;\n\n  // Remove scripts that reference stripped internal files\n  if (pkg.scripts) {\n    for (const script of STRIP_SCRIPTS) {\n      delete pkg.scripts[script];\n    }\n  }\n\n  await writeFile(packagePath, JSON.stringify(pkg, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n  // ... logging","numLines":40,"startLine":340,"totalLines":872}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:59:21.490Z"}
