{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016RpEg5u4LoHcD19p1HBQAW","type":"tool_result","content":"   770→\n   771→4. **Build executable.** `build-executable.ts` uses `ENTRY_POINT = \"server/index.ts\"` and builds from root. This path doesn't change with workspace addition.\n   772→\n   773→5. **Cross-runtime tests.** `run-cross-runtime-tests.ts` resolves `testsDir` from `import.meta.dirname`. This path doesn't change.\n   774→\n   775→6. **Cross-platform path separators.** The CI matrix includes Windows, macOS, and Linux. Workspace paths are resolved by Bun which handles path separators. No issues expected, but worth monitoring the first CI run after migration.\n   776→\n   777→7. **Root `tsconfig.json` include scope.** The `include: [\"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\"]` glob picks up everything in the repo tree. Without `\"docs/**/*\"` in `exclude`, `bun run tc` will fail on docs files (incompatible compiler options). This is addressed in Phase 2, Step 2.1, but listed here as an edge case because it is easy to miss in future workspace additions — any new workspace with TypeScript files will need the same exclude entry.\n   778→\n   779→8. **Biome scope does not cover scripts.** The `biome.json` `includes` list covers `server/**/*`, `tests/e2e/**/*`, `tests/utils/**/*`, `tests/unit/**/*`, and `types/**/*`. The `scripts/` directory is not included. This means the changes to `sync-public.ts`, `release.ts`, `test-sync-local.ts`, and `generate-schemas.ts` will not be linted by Biome. This is existing behavior, not a regression — just noting it so the implementing agent does not expect Biome to catch formatting issues in modified scripts.\n   780→\n   781→9. **`bunfig.toml` workspace scope.** The root `bunfig.toml` has only a `[test.env]` section setting `BUN_TEST = \"true\"`. This env var is consumed by `isNonInteractive()` in the runtime's `execution-setup.ts` to skip confirmation prompts during tests. It applies to `bun test` runs from the root, but all test scripts (`test:unit`, `test:integration`, etc.) are path-scoped to specific directories (`tests/unit`, `tests/integration`, etc.) and will not pick up docs files. No `bunfig.toml` changes are needed. The implementing agent should verify this remains true if the docs workspace ever adds its own test scripts.\n   782→\n   783→### CI enhancement (optional, recommended)\n   784→\n   785→Consider adding a docs build step to CI to prevent monorepo PRs from silently breaking docs:\n   786→\n   787→```yaml\n   788→# In ci.yml, add a new job:\n   789→docs-build:\n   790→  name: Docs Build Check\n   791→  runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n   792→  timeout-minutes: 10\n   793→  steps:\n   794→    - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n   795→    - uses: ./.github/actions/setup-environment\n   796→      with:\n   797→        install-gemini: \"false\"\n   798→    - name: Build docs\n   799→      run: cd docs && bun run build\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a5d48287-fa06-41ff-8c53-7bb7d1a349eb","uuid":"24c8ef95-c420-4243-b001-c442179f1c34","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"\n4. **Build executable.** `build-executable.ts` uses `ENTRY_POINT = \"server/index.ts\"` and builds from root. This path doesn't change with workspace addition.\n\n5. **Cross-runtime tests.** `run-cross-runtime-tests.ts` resolves `testsDir` from `import.meta.dirname`. This path doesn't change.\n\n6. **Cross-platform path separators.** The CI matrix includes Windows, macOS, and Linux. Workspace paths are resolved by Bun which handles path separators. No issues expected, but worth monitoring the first CI run after migration.\n\n7. **Root `tsconfig.json` include scope.** The `include: [\"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\"]` glob picks up everything in the repo tree. Without `\"docs/**/*\"` in `exclude`, `bun run tc` will fail on docs files (incompatible compiler options). This is addressed in Phase 2, Step 2.1, but listed here as an edge case because it is easy to miss in future workspace additions — any new workspace with TypeScript files will need the same exclude entry.\n\n8. **Biome scope does not cover scripts.** The `biome.json` `includes` list covers `server/**/*`, `tests/e2e/**/*`, `tests/utils/**/*`, `tests/unit/**/*`, and `types/**/*`. The `scripts/` directory is not included. This means the changes to `sync-public.ts`, `release.ts`, `test-sync-local.ts`, and `generate-schemas.ts` will not be linted by Biome. This is existing behavior, not a regression — just noting it so the implementing agent does not expect Biome to catch formatting issues in modified scripts.\n\n9. **`bunfig.toml` workspace scope.** The root `bunfig.toml` has only a `[test.env]` section setting `BUN_TEST = \"true\"`. This env var is consumed by `isNonInteractive()` in the runtime's `execution-setup.ts` to skip confirmation prompts during tests. It applies to `bun test` runs from the root, but all test scripts (`test:unit`, `test:integration`, etc.) are path-scoped to specific directories (`tests/unit`, `tests/integration`, etc.) and will not pick up docs files. No `bunfig.toml` changes are needed. The implementing agent should verify this remains true if the docs workspace ever adds its own test scripts.\n\n### CI enhancement (optional, recommended)\n\nConsider adding a docs build step to CI to prevent monorepo PRs from silently breaking docs:\n\n```yaml\n# In ci.yml, add a new job:\ndocs-build:\n  name: Docs Build Check\n  runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n  timeout-minutes: 10\n  steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n    - uses: ./.github/actions/setup-environment\n      with:\n        install-gemini: \"false\"\n    - name: Build docs\n      run: cd docs && bun run build","numLines":30,"startLine":770,"totalLines":872}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:59:25.758Z"}
