{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JRaN57zky8EAZjcp3Ryatk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tasks are complete. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n## What Changed\n\nThe blind review (`plan/reviews/current/review.md`) raised 18 items against the plan. I verified each against the actual source code and made 13 targeted edits to `plan/merged/plan.md`:\n\n**Substantive changes:**\n1. **Phase 8 reordered** — Archive step moved from 8.1 to 8.4 (last), since you can't archive the old repo before the PR is even opened. Commit is now 8.1, PR is 8.2.\n2. **Explicit `git add bun.lock`** added to the commit step, plus a line in the commit message template. Without this, CI's `--frozen-lockfile` would fail.\n3. **Vercel root directory strategy swapped** — Repo-root (`/`) with `cd docs && bun run build` is now the primary approach. The `docs/`-as-root option is documented as an optimization to try afterward. Bun workspace resolution from a subdirectory in Vercel is not well-documented.\n4. **CVE env var reframed as human-approval gate** — The implementing agent cannot determine if `DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969` is intentional. Phase 7 needs explicit human sign-off.\n\n**Precision improvements:**\n5. `STRIP_DIRS` coverage now names all three consumers (`prepareSnapshot()`, `initialSync()`, `snapshotSync()`)\n6. `docsAvailable` comment corrected to reference `docs/public/` (not `docs/`)\n7. `.gitignore` explanation now describes tree-wide matching semantics\n8. `bunfig.toml` verification added as edge case item 9\n9. Assumption #1 tightened to state default is simple file copy\n\n**One disagreement:** Review Item 17 assumed a `.gitignore` exists inside `nextra-site/` — I verified it does not. Added clarifying notes instead.\n\nAll changes and reasoning are documented in `plan/review/current/updation_thoughts_and_changes.md`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens